    "Notes Updated": "8/30/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Fastball is now up to 96, and sitting 92 94 MPH, think he's mostly throwing a 4FB, but may be mixing a 2FB in at times\n Formerly referred to as a curveball, the breaking ball is probably more of a slider, a little slurvy.\n He is super comfortable landing the BB for strikes or throwing out of the zone for chase, sits 82 84 but drops down to 79 at times, especially later in starts\n Changeup is in the 84 86 range and seems comfortable landing for strikes and getting chase as well, has a lot of fade to it\n Command and control show signs of being solid down the road, but the walks have been too high right now\n One of my favorite under the radar arms in the org currently",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/25/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Already was touching 92 mph on fastball at 16.\n  Changeup that flashes plus potential.\n  Curveball that could develop into an average or better pitch.\n  Looks to be a fly ball pitcher who had some HR issues in his first pro season.\n  Strikeout to walk ratio is not bad. Definitely one I will watch next year.",
